{"tool_name":"rhythmicdb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"rhythmicdb","home":"http://rhythmicdb.css-mendel.it","summary":"Database of circadian and ultradian transcripts in control tissues of kingdom-wide species.","addition_date":"2022-09-29T21:04:39.121784Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:33:47.024784Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:rhythmicdb","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"g.mazzoccoli@operapadrepio.it","name":"Gianluigi Mazzoccoli","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"t.mazza@operapadrepio.it","name":"Tommaso Mazza","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Andrea Cabibbo"},{"name":"Francesco Petrizzelli"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"},{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"},{"term":"Repeat sequence organisation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0380"}]}],"name":"RhythmicDB","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.3389/fgene.2022.882044","metadata":{"abstract":"The physiology and behavior of living organisms are featured by time-related variations driven by molecular clockworks that arose during evolution stochastically and heterogeneously. Over the years, several high-throughput experiments were performed to evaluate time-dependent gene expression in different cell types across several species and experimental conditions. Here, these were retrieved, manually curated, and analyzed by two software packages, BioCycle and MetaCycle, to infer circadian or ultradian transcripts across different species. These transcripts were stored in RhythmicDB and made publically available.","authors":[{"name":"Biagini T."},{"name":"Cabibbo A."},{"name":"Castellana S."},{"name":"Mazza T."},{"name":"Mazzoccoli G."},{"name":"Petrizzelli F."}],"citationCount":6